There is a category of keypads available in various sizes known as "matrix keypads." They are called this because they are viewed and utilized as a matrix.
The number of pins on these keypads is equal to the sum of their rows and columns. For example, a 4x4 keypad with 16 keys can be controlled using 8 pins.
